  "description": "The proposal, under the application of 1a Ranelagh Cottages, including the following:\n\n•  The construction of a shared classical portico to the principal entrance, incorporating a pair of plasters, entablature, and rosettes, detailed in accordance with local materials. \n\n•. Retention of existing boundary walls and brick paving, including a small pathway currently owned by the Grosvenor Estate, but is in negotiations to obtain ownership. \n\n•. Installation of new stone paving and steps to provide a more legible entrance.\n\n\nThe porch / portico will be constructed from blockwork and timber with a stuccoed / rendered finish externally and all associated joinery items relating to the alterations on the north elevation will be made traditionally to be in keeping with the prevailing characteristics and materials. \n\nThere are no TPO trees registered on the site or proposed to be removed in this scheme. \n",
